Social Status
------------------------------------------------------
Version:		1.20.3
APIVersion: 	100026
Authors:		Alyka & BinaryHeart

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Description
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Allows you to log into Elder Scrolls Online with a defined Social Status:

	Online;
	Away From Keyboard;
	Do Not Disturb;
	Offline.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Options
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Social Status' options are in the AddonSettings menu:

	Main Menu > Settings > Addon Settings > Social Status

There are three options that can be set:

Account Social Status (defaults to Offline)
[
	Online
	Away From Keyboard
	Do Not Disturb
	Offline
]

Each time you log into Elder Scrolls Online your Social Status will be set to this option, unless you've chosen to override it for the character you've logged on as. Changing this option on any character will affect the Social Status you logon with for ALL characters whose Social Status is set to Account.

Current Character's Social Status (defaults to Account)
[
	Online
	Away From Keyboard
	Do Not Disturb
	Offline
	Account
]

Provides a means to override Account Social Status whenever you log onto the character you changed this setting on. A value of Account, which is the default value, will log you on with the option chosen for Account Social Status.

Fix activity bug (defaults to OFF)
[
	ON
	OFF
]

If you're disconnected from the server because of inactivity while you appear offline, there's a miniscule chance you'll end up in a broken state on rosters when you log back in (showing at the top guild and friend lists as offline, without any character and last online time equal to the amount of time you've been logged on). This chance is significantly greater if you timeout from the character select. When you end up in this state and this option is set to ON, Social Status will attempt to fix this and put you back in a proper offline state. When it works, you'll show as having been offline since you last set your status to online and on that character. Around half of the time it won't work and you'll briefly appear online, which is why this is turned off as default.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Slash Commands
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
You can enter the following slash commands into the chat box to set your Social Status:

	/online		- Social Status = Online
	/afk		- Toggle your Social Status between [Away From Keyboard\previous Social Status before afk toggled]
	/dnd		- Social Status = Do Not Disturb
	/offine		- Social Status = Offline

To check your Social Status without opening your Social Panel (Zeni default keybinding O):

	/socialstatus
	/ss

To quickly navigate to the Options menu:

	/sso

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Installation
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Extract archive to your Elder Scrolls Online Addons folder:

	On Windows:	C:\Users\<username>\Documents\Elder Scrolls Online\<version>\AddOns
	On Mac:		~/Documents/Elder Scrolls Online/<version>/AddOns (or get a Windows PC =P )

Replace <version> with "live" if you're playing on the NA server and "liveeu" if you're on the EU server (without quotations).

On Windows, <username> is the user profile you log onto Windows with
	e.g.	My Windows path would be:	C:\Users\Fran\Documents\Elder Scrolls Online\liveeu\AddOns

Ingame, go to your SETTINGS > ADD-ONS menu and ensure Social Status is checked

Have fun! =)

